.Sh EX OPTIONS
.Bd -literal -compact
Ex options are ex commands designed to alter global variables.
Variables hold a signed integer. Argument sets the value. A non-numeric
argument yields its first byte. No argument logically inverts
the current value, unless stated otherwise.

Argument notation shows the default value.
.Ed

.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
